{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Best of Bread and The Very Best Of Fleetwood Mac feel like natural next choices because I want melodic, approachable songs that connect with my interest in Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and The Cars.",
    "Chronicle and The Guess Who fit my repeated interest in older rock and retrospective collections, especially alongside my mid-sixties and classic rock listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele connects with my occasional newer pop listening, but that is less appealing today than older hits collections.",
    "Fm - Greatest Hits and It's the Girls! leave me unsure what music I would be choosing, so I do not have enough confidence that they match my interests.",
    "Styx and Journey fit my broader rock interests, but their bigger rock sound is less appealing right now than the softer collections; the fifties collection also reaches earlier than the sixties and seventies music I currently want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits collection is appealing only when the music itself fits; that shared label alone does not make me want an album.",
    "My interest in classic rock does not mean I am equally ready for every rock sound or every older decade."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The mellow, melodic appeal of Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards matters to my choices today, making Bread especially attractive.",
    "My occasional interest in newer pop does not outweigh my repeated interest in older hits, and even a plausible rock match may be something I save for another visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in classic hits, but sometimes overlooked my current preference for softer, melodic sixties and seventies music."
}"}
